s.", "model_design": "Replace the LightGBM ensemble with a DistilRoBERTa model (distilroberta-base) for its smaller size and speed. Modify the model to accept both tokenized input IDs/attention masks and a separate statistical feature vector. After obtaining the pooled output (CLS token) from DistilRoBERTa, pass the statistical features through a small MLP (linear->ReLU->linear, output 64 dimensions), concatenate with the pooled output (768+64=832), and then feed into the final classifier head (832->256->3 with GELU activation and 0.2 dropout). During training, implement Multi-Sample Dropout (4 forward passes with different dropout masks, average logits before loss computation) to regularize, as successful historical experiments did. Keep cross-entropy loss with label smoothing (0.1).", "training_evaluation": "Replace the 5-fold CV training loop with a single stratified 80/20 split (as per initial plan). Use AdamW optimizer (lr=2e-5), linear warmup over 10% of steps, and cosine annealing schedule decaying to 1e-6 (from successful experiments). Train for 8 epochs with batch size 32, early stopping on validation log loss (patience=3). Use mixed precision (AMP) to speed up. Save the best model checkpoint. For inference, load the best model, run on test set with no gradient computation, apply softmax to logits, and save submission. This addresses overfitting and follows the successful training recipe from historical experiments."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
